{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00753",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 1.57,
      "end_seconds": 12.34,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'm Rosa, I'm Mr Quinn's carer, and this is his son, Danny. We're worried about his tiredness and his skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.53,
      "end_seconds": 22.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Hello Rosa, hello Danny, hello Mr Quinn. Tell me what you've noticed. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.88,
      "end_seconds": 28.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I'm fine. A bit tired, that's all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 31.28,
      "end_seconds": 43.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.58,
      "text": "He's more than a bit tired, Dad. He's been exhausted for months, and his skin is going dark, especially his hands, and around his elbows."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.82,
      "end_seconds": 51.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Mr Quinn, when did the tiredness start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.65,
      "end_seconds": 58.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "Oh, I couldn't say, I've been slow for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.0,
      "end_seconds": 65.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "And the darker skin, did you notice it, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.54,
      "end_seconds": 76.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.8,
      "text": "I haven't noticed it. Danny's the one who points it out. I couldn't tell you when."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 78.0,
      "end_seconds": 86.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "I noticed it in the spring, in his palm creases, but I'm not sure when exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.31,
      "end_seconds": 97.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "I'll note that none of you can pin it down. Mr Quinn, any dizziness, especially when you stand up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.88,
      "end_seconds": 101.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "No. No dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 103.15,
      "end_seconds": 113.22,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "He does get dizzy, doctor. He held the wall twice last week, getting up from the chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 114.28,
      "end_seconds": 118.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "And he nearly fell in the bathroom."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.72,
      "end_seconds": 130.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "I'll record that Mr Quinn says no, and Rosa and Danny say yes. What medicines does he take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 133.8,
      "end_seconds": 148.56,
      "duration_seconds": 14.76,
      "text": "Just the hydrocortisone, 10 mg in the morning and 5 mg in the afternoon, but I'm not sure he's been taking the afternoon dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.78,
      "end_seconds": 152.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone, for what condition?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 153.39,
      "end_seconds": 156.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Addison's disease, diagnosed ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.85,
      "end_seconds": 161.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "And is there anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 163.74,
      "end_seconds": 165.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Underactive thyroid too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.88,
      "end_seconds": 173.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Mr Quinn, are you taking your hydrocortisone? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.32,
      "end_seconds": 182.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Mostly. I forget the afternoon ones, I'm sure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.83,
      "end_seconds": 189.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "I'll check. Is there any vomiting, diarrhoea, or weight loss? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.76,
      "end_seconds": 196.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "A bit of nausea. Nothing else. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.82,
      "end_seconds": 207.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.99,
      "text": "Let me check his chest and pulse, and I'd like to check his blood pressure sitting and standing. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 209.04,
      "end_seconds": 213.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "He's quite wobbly on his feet. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.32,
      "end_seconds": 229.87,
      "duration_seconds": 13.55,
      "text": "Right. Because of the possible dizziness, the dark skin, and the missed doses, I'd say this looks like his Addison's disease is under-treated, an adrenal problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 231.67,
      "end_seconds": 234.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Is that dangerous? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.22,
      "end_seconds": 252.89,
      "duration_seconds": 16.67,
      "text": "It can be, if it gets worse, because a low steroid level can cause a crisis. I'd like to arrange blood tests today, to check his sodium, potassium and cortisol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 254.49,
      "end_seconds": 258.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "We can do it now? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.98,
      "end_seconds": 268.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "Yes. Please make sure he takes his hydrocortisone, including the afternoon dose, and use a pill box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 269.95,
      "end_seconds": 273.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "I'll set the alarms. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.95,
      "end_seconds": 287.25,
      "duration_seconds": 11.3,
      "text": "And if he's vomiting, very dizzy, confused, or collapses, take him straight to the emergency department, and tell them he has Addison's."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.24,
      "end_seconds": 294.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "I carry a steroid card. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.86,
      "end_seconds": 301.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Good. I'd like to see you again in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 303.52,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "We'll be there. ~"
    }
  ]
}
